hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23619","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Shu'bah, Yahya ibn Husayn ibn Urwah narrated to us, he said: My grandmother narrated to me, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: If a slave is appointed over you leading you by the Book of Allah, then listen to him and obey."
"23620","Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Yahya ibn Husayn from his grandmother, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: May Allah have mercy on those who shave, may Allah have mercy on those who shave, may Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said the third time: And those who shorten? He said: And those who shorten."
"23621","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur ibn Hayyan al-Asadi from Ibn Bijad from his grandmother, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Return the beggar even with a burnt sheep's trotter."
